<section>
  <exercises>
    <heading level="1">Section 10.4 Exercises</heading>
    <heading level="1">Practice Makes Perfect</heading>
    <paragraph>Use the Properties of Logarithms</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, use the properties of logarithms to evaluate.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="218" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$\log_{4}1$$ ⓑ $$\log_{8}8$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="219" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$\log_{12}1$$ ⓑ $$\ln e$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ 0 ⓑ 1</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="220" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$3^{\log_{3}6}$$ ⓑ $$\log_{2}2^{7}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="221" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$5^{\log_{5}10}$$ ⓑ $$\log_{4}4^{10}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ 10 ⓑ 10</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="222" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$8^{\log_{8}7}$$ ⓑ $$\log_{6}6^{-2}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="223" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$6^{\log_{6}15}$$ ⓑ $$\log_{8}8^{-4}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ 15 ⓑ $$-4-4$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="224" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$10^{\log \sqrt{5}}$$ ⓑ $$\log 10^{-2}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="225" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$10^{\log \sqrt{3}}$$ ⓑ $$\log 10^{-1}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$33$$ ⓑ $$-1-1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="226" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$e^{\ln 4}$$ ⓑ $$\ln e^{2}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="227" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>ⓐ $$e^{\ln 3}$$ ⓑ $$\ln e^{7}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>ⓐ 3 ⓑ 7</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, use the Product Property of Logarithms to write each logarithm as a sum of logarithms. Simplify if possible.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="228" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{4}6x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="229" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{5}8y$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$log 5 8 + log 5 y log 5 8 + log 5 y$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="230" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{2}32xy$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="231" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{3}81xy$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$4 + log 3 x + log 3 y 4 + log 3 x + log 3 y$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="232" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log 100x$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="233" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log 1000y$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$3 + log y 3 + log y$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, use the Quotient Property of Logarithms to write each logarithm as a sum of logarithms. Simplify if possible.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="234" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{3}\frac{3}{8}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="235" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{6}\frac{5}{6}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$log 6 5 - 1 log 6 5 - 1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="236" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{4}\frac{16}{y}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="237" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{5}\frac{125}{x}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$3 - log 5 x 3 - log 5 x$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="238" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log \frac{x}{10}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="239" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log \frac{10,000}{y}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$4 - log y 4 - log y$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="240" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\ln \frac{e^{3}}{3}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="241" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\ln \frac{e^{4}}{16}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$4 - ln 16 4 - ln 16$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, use the Power Property of Logarithms to expand each. Simplify if possible.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="242" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{3}x^{2}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="243" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{2}x^{5}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$5 log 2 x 5 log 2 x$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="244" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log x^{-2}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="245" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log x^{-3}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$-3 log x -3 log x$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="246" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{4}\sqrt{x}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="247" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{5}\sqrt[3]{x}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$1 3 log 5 x 1 3 log 5 x$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="248" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\ln x^{\sqrt{3}}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="249" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\ln x^{\sqrt[3]{4}}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$4 3 ln x 4 3 ln x$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, use the Properties of Logarithms to expand the logarithm. Simplify if possible.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="250" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{5}\left( {4x^{6}y^{4}} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="251" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{2}\left( {3x^{5}y^{3}} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$log 2 3 + 5 log 2 x + 3 log 2 y log 2 3 + 5 log 2 x + 3 log 2 y$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="252" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{3}\left( {\sqrt{2}x^{2}} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="253" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{5}\left( {\sqrt[4]{21}y^{3}} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$1 4 log 5 21 + 3 log 5 y 1 4 log 5 21 + 3 log 5 y$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="254" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{3}\frac{xy^{2}}{z^{2}}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="255" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{5}\frac{4ab^{3}c^{4}}{d^{2}}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$log 5 4 + log 5 a + 3 log 5 b log 5 4 + log 5 a + 3 log 5 b$$ $$+ 4 log 5 c - 2 log 5 d + 4 log 5 c - 2 log 5 d$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="256" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{4}\frac{\sqrt{x}}{16y^{4}}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="257" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{3}\frac{\sqrt[3]{x^{2}}}{27y^{4}}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$2 3 log 3 x - 3 - 4 log 3 y 2 3 log 3 x - 3 - 4 log 3 y$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="258" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{2}\frac{\sqrt{2x + y^{2}}}{z^{2}}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="259" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{3}\frac{\sqrt{3x + 2y^{2}}}{5z^{2}}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$1 2 log 3 ( 3 x + 2 y 2 ) - log 3 5 - 2 log 3 z 1 2 log 3 ( 3 x + 2 y 2 ) - log 3 5 - 2 log 3 z$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="260" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{2}\sqrt[4]{\frac{5x^{3}}{2y^{2}z^{4}}}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="261" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{5}\sqrt[3]{\frac{3x^{2}}{4y^{3}z}}$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$1 3 ( log 5 3 + 2 log 5 x - log 5 4 1 3 ( log 5 3 + 2 log 5 x - log 5 4$$ $$- 3 log 5 y - log 5 z ) - 3 log 5 y - log 5 z )$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, use the Properties of Logarithms to condense the logarithm. Simplify if possible.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="262" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{6}4 + \log_{6}9$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="263" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log 4 + \log 25$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>2</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="264" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{2}80 - \log_{2}5$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="265" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{3}36 - \log_{3}4$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>2</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="266" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{3}4 + \log_{3}\left( {x + 1} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="267" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{2}5 - \log_{2}\left( {x - 1} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$log 2 5 x - 1 log 2 5 x - 1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="268" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{7}3 + \log_{7}x - \log_{7}y$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="269" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{5}2 - \log_{5}x - \log_{5}y$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$log 5 2 x y log 5 2 x y$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="270" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$4\log_{2}x + 6\log_{2}y$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="271" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$6\log_{3}x + 9\log_{3}y$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$log 3 x 6 y 9 log 3 x 6 y 9$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="272" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{3}\left( {x^{2} - 1} \right) - 2\log_{3}\left( {x - 1} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="273" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log \left( {x^{2} + 2x + 1} \right) - 2\log \left( {x + 1} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>0</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="274" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$4\log x - 2\log y - 3\log z$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="275" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$3\ln x + 4\ln y - 2\ln z$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$ln x 3 y 4 z 2 ln x 3 y 4 z 2$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="276" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\frac{1}{3}\log x - 3\log \left( {x + 1} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="277" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$2\log \left( {2x + 3} \right) + \frac{1}{2}\log \left( {x + 1} \right)$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$log ( 2 x + 3 ) 2 \cdot x + 1 log ( 2 x + 3 ) 2 \cdot x + 1$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <paragraph>Use the Change-of-Base Formula</paragraph>
    <paragraph>In the following exercises, use the Change-of-Base Formula, rounding to three decimal places, to approximate each logarithm.</paragraph>
    <exercise number="278" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{3}42$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="279" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{5}46$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$2.379 2.379$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="280" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{12}87$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="281" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{15}93$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$1.674 1.674$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="282" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{\sqrt{2}}17$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="283" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>$$\log_{\sqrt{3}}21$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>$$5.542 5.542$$</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <heading level="1">Writing Exercises</heading>
    <exercise number="284" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Write the Product Property in your own words. Does it apply to each of the following? $$\log_{a}5x,$$ $$\log_{a}\left( {5 + x} \right).$$ Why or why not?</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="285" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Write the Power Property in your own words. Does it apply to each of the following? $$\log_{a}x^{p},$$ $$\left( {\log_{a}x} \right)^{r}.$$ Why or why not?</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>Answers will vary.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="286" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Use an example to show that $$\log \left( {a + b} \right) \neq \log a + \log b.$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="287" has_solution="true">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Explain how to find the value of $$\log_{7}15$$ using your calculator.</paragraph>
      </problem>
      <solution>
        <paragraph>Answers will vary.</paragraph>
      </solution>
    </exercise>
    <heading level="1">Self Check</heading>
    <paragraph>ⓐ After completing the exercises, use this checklist to evaluate your mastery of the objectives of this section.</paragraph>
    <paragraph>ⓑ On a scale of $$1 - 10,$$ how would you rate your mastery of this section in light of your responses on the checklist? How can you improve this?</paragraph>
  </exercises>
</section>
